    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T21:10:39Z",
    "body": "PR #2023 (for #1993) adds a lathe view frame to the viewport camera. On a lathe the spindle axis (world Z) is horizontal, +Z to the right, and the cross-slide (world X) is up. The frame comes from the machine kind (`crates/ui/src/view_frame.rs`, `ViewFrame::for_kind`). A mill machine again restores the milling view.\n\nThis issue still needs:\n\n- The world gizmo: show Z and X only on a lathe, and Y only when the machine has a Y axis.\n- A decision for mill-turn machines. PR #2023 keeps them in the milling frame.\n- View cube face names for the lathe frame, if necessary. The cube names world directions in each frame.\n- A test that the posted program of a turning golden does not change.\n\nA stacked PR can build on the branch `issue/1993-lathe-envelope-axis`. This comment does not close this issue.",
